{"id":"u-7dbf83e9-9e92-45b2-86d5-74de7bc67990","src":"community","title":"OMNIMAN SPLIT (4-Day U/L + cardio)","author":"Jay B","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/SARaK2-omniman-split-4-day-ul-cardio","desc":"9-Week Hybrid Athlete Block: Strength + Aesthetics + Conditioning\nA 4-day Upper/Lower block built for intermediate lifters who want to break a plateau and train as a complete athlete. Squat, Bench, and Deadlift each get a dedicated focus day. Periodized across 9 weeks with a mandatory deload built in.\nStructure:\n\t•\t4 lifting days/week, ~75 min each\n\t•\t3 HIIT sessions/week, ~20 min each (assault bike, rower, stairmaster, turf sprints)\n\t•\t3 ab routines integrated across the week\n\t•\t12-15 working sets per major muscle group weekly\n\t•\tRPE-based prescriptions for autoregulation\n9-Week Periodization:\n\t•\tWeeks 1-3: Volume accumulation (5-8 reps, RPE 7-8)\n\t•\tWeeks 4-6: Intensity (3-5 reps, RPE 8-9)\n\t•\tWeeks 7-8: Peak + PR test (1-3 reps, RPE 9-10)\n\t•\tWeek 9: Deload\nTotal weekly time: ~6 hours\nBest for:\n\t•\tIntermediate lifters with 1+ year of consistent training\n\t•\tAnyone stuck on the same program for 6+ months\n\t•\tLifters chasing strength without sacrificing size\n\t•\tHybrid athlete goals (strength, conditioning, aesthetics)\nNot for:\n\t•\tPure novices (you’ll progress faster on simpler programs)\n\t•\tPowerlifters peaking for a meet (too much accessory volume)\n\t•\tAnyone training fewer than 4 days/week\nWhat’s different:\nMost programs let you grind near-max RPE indefinitely without a programmed deload. That’s how plateaus build. This block varies intensity by phase and forces a real deload at Week 9 to clear accumulated fatigue. It’s the missing piece in most hybrid programming.\nEquipment: Full gym access (barbells, dumbbells, cables, machines, conditioning equipment).​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":80,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":